  "notes": "{迷|まよ}う describes being lost (physically) or uncertain/hesitant (mentally).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{迷|まよ}っている indicates an ongoing state of being lost or indecisive: ⟦まだ→まだ：00603_mada⟧{迷|まよ}っている (I'm still undecided).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{迷|まよ}う: to get lost (on the way)\n- 〜か〜か{迷|まよ}う: to be torn between ~ and ~\n- {迷|まよ}わず: without hesitation\n- ⟦{答|こた}え→答え：00790_kotae⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{迷|まよ}う: to be at a loss for an answer\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{迷|まよ}い→迷い：19437_mayoi⟧: hesitation, doubt, wavering\n- ⟦{迷子|まいご}→迷子：03729_maigo⟧: lost child\n- ⟦{迷|めい}{惑|わく}→迷惑：02432_meiwaku⟧: trouble, annoyance, nuisance\n- ⟦{迷信|めいしん}→迷信：09212_meishin⟧: superstition\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{悩|なや}む→悩む：02380_nayamu⟧: to be troubled, worried (deeper emotional struggle)\n- {迷|まよ}う: to be unsure, hesitant (about a choice)",
